      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-46846",
      ":question/problem": "Daniel surveys $625$ Orlando citizens and records their ages. The table below shows the results of his survey.\n\n| Age (years) | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Less than $5$ years old | $55$ |\n| $5$-$11$ | $85$ |\n| $12$-$15$ | $95$ |\n| $16$-$20$ | $140$ |\n| $21$-$30$ | $100$ |\n| $31$-$46$ | $70$ |\n| More than $46$ | $80$ |\n\nTampa has an estimated population of $393000$. Assuming that the distribution of ages is the same for both cities, estimate, to the nearest thousand, the number of citizens with ages between $21$ and $30$ years old in Tampa.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
